From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:06:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave a theme's conditions on the system out quietly without
 one

A theme is also read without a system, for the menus. A condition on
a system variable ({system.name} == 'x', in a variables block or on a
property) then has nothing to compare and was logged as an invalid
expression, once per condition at every theme load. It is left out
as before, with a debug line instead of an error.
---
 es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp b/es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp
index 49be5398..dd3a7339 100644
--- a/es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp
@@ -1210,7 +1210,14 @@ bool ThemeData::parseFilterAttributes(const pugi::xml_node& node)
 			}
 			catch (std::domain_error& e)
 			{
-				LOG(LogError) << "if \"" << ifAttribute << "\" expression is invalid : " << e.what();
+				// A theme read without a system (the menus' theme) has no system variables: a condition on one only
+				// leaves its part out there
+				if (mEvaluatorVariables.find("system.name") == mEvaluatorVariables.cend() && ifAttribute.find("{system.") != std::string::npos &&
+					std::string(e.what()).find("Unable to find the variable 'system.") == 0)
+					LOG(LogDebug) << "if \"" << ifAttribute << "\" left out: no system";
+				else
+					LOG(LogError) << "if \"" << ifAttribute << "\" expression is invalid : " << e.what();
+
 				return false;
 			}
 		}
